RF.put("questb:b65",{"8625":{"id":8625,"t":"Enigma Shoulderpads","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Bronze Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Death Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nEnigma Shoulderpads\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Mage Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8625\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Enigma Shoulderpads this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Bronze Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8705":{"id":8705,"t":"Gavel of Infinite Wisdom","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ornate Hilt, 2 Lambent Idols, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ornate Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Lambent Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nGavel of Infinite Wisdom\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8545":{"id":8545,"t":"The Horde Needs Mithril Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 52.","obj":"Bring 20 Mithril Bars to Senior Sergeant T'kelah at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Mithril Bar","desc":"‹class›, the war it is comin' and the only thing we can do is prepare for it. That be where you and I can help each other, mon. Ya see, they put me in charge of collectin' all the mithril bars we be needin' ta build for all the things we gonna need. An I still be needin' more!\nSo, I be hopin' that you can get out there an mine us up some mithril, then smelt it into bars. Sound like something you can do for us?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"It sure would be nice to be havin' all of the mithril bars that we be needin' for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort. Is that why you be back, mon? You got my bars?","done":"This be a good start for you an me, ‹class›. That be another twenty mithril bars that I can be puttin' on the stacks an checkin' off of the list. It all gonna be put to good use makin' the war materiel.\nBe makin' sure that you check back in with me 'cuz you know it be lookin' like we gonna need even more of those mithril bars.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Senior Sergeant T'kelah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6545":{"id":6545,"t":"Warsong Runner Update","lv":19,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warsong Report","rew":"You will receive:\nWarsong Runner Update","back":"So you're here with my orders? Always good to see a new recruit with an exuberant nature and a strong will.\nYou'd best learn fast if you expect to keep up here. The threat of the naga grows, ‹name›. I have observed and have taken up defenses against several attacks on this outpost since I arrived here.\nBut if you'd like to pitch in with that effort, speak with one of the others here at the outpost.","done":"Well, my update will explain all of this to Kadrak. You must return this to him as quickly as possible.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":12.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Warsong Runner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1025":{"id":1025,"t":"An Aggressive Defense","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 1 Den Watcher, 2 Ursas, 10 Totemics, and 12 Warriors of the Foulweald tribe, and then return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\nFoulweald Den Watcher slain\nFoulweald Ursa slain : 0/ 2\nFoulweald Totemic slain : 0/ 10\nFoulweald Warrior slain : 0/ 12","desc":"Before you travel to the moonwell I have another task that will aid the people of Ashenvale if you would like to test your skills.\nAlong the road heading east before the Falfarren River, furbolgs have been attacking travelers. Their tortured minds feeding upon fear, and their appetites satiated by the blood of innocents.\nAid the Sentinels in protecting the lands by showing those monsters the same mercy they have shown our kind.\nI believe their camps are south of the road... be careful.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Moist Cornbread 10 Melon Juice\nMoney: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The furbolg were not always our enemy, ‹name›. But times change, and it is no longer a time of peace here in these dark woods.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"705":{"id":705,"t":"Pearl Diving","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 9 Blue Pearls to Rigglefuzz in the Badlands.\n9 Blue Pearl Giant Clam","desc":"The Badlands is a harsh place, filled with vicious predators and bold scavengers. Scary, especially for a short little goblin. To survive, I have to be tricky!\nI know the recipe for flash bombs. I use those to scare away wildlife. But I'm running low on one of the ingredients: crushed blue pearl powder. Get me some and I'll make it worth your efforts.\nHeh, and I hope you have good boots on. The Blue Pearls I need are found from clams at the Vile Reef.\nYep, the Vile Reef in Stranglethorn!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlash Rifle Flash Wand\nYou will also receive:\nFlash Bomb\nExperience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Did you get my pearls? I'm almost out of flash bombs!","done":"These will work great! I just need to smash them into powder...then mix them with a little of this and a little of that.\nWatch out, scavengers! Prepare to be flashed!\nBadlands Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":42.4,"y":52.9,"n":"Rigglefuzz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"3825":{"id":3825,"t":"Ogre Head On A Stick = Party","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Gor'tesh's Lopped Off Head and place it at the top of Dreadmaul Rock. Look for a soft dirt mound to plant the pike.\nGor'tesh Head Planted\nProvided: Gor'tesh's Lopped Off Head","desc":"Just one last thing you must do, soldier.\nI've taken the liberty of putting Gor'tesh's head on a pike. Now all you have to do is take this head to the top of Dreadmaul Rock and stick it into the ground. Once you do that, watch as those cowardly ogres run for their lives! After you've had your fun, come back to me and I'll reward you for all of your hard work.\n<Oralius seems to be losing touch with reality.>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMaddening Gauntlets Choking Band\nMoney: 2 40 2 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"So? Did you paint any pictures of the event?","done":"Outstanding work, soldier! Simply amazing! Oh I'll get the medal of bravery for this, er, I mean you'll be rewarded handsomely for this!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Oralius","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97905":{"id":97905,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Jandi in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"Dere ya have it, ya be craftin' your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't be carin' much for camps being set up in da center of town, so ya be needin' ta head into da wilderness if ya be wantin' to try it out.\nNo camp is complete without a campfire, mon. Ya be needin' one of dose before ya be startin' up your camp. Most cooks be teachin' ya ta make a fire. Check in with someone who can train ya in da culinary arts if ya haven't already learned da basics.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.4,"y":39.6,"n":"Jandi","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94225":{"id":94225,"t":"Craftsmans writ rough bronze leggings","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Rough Bronze Leggings\nRough Bronze Leggings","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Rough Bronze Leggings, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"What's up?","done":"These are the leggings I ordered, huh? \"Three to five business days,\" they said. More like three to five business MONTHS!\nI submitted this when I was working for the Venture Co out there, and let me just say, that partnership is well over with, so we can consider this order expired.\nWhy aren't you leaving yet? Ugh, fine! Here's your payment.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94305":{"id":94305,"t":"Craftsmans writ shadoweave gloves","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Shadoweave Gloves\nShadoweave Gloves","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Shadoweave Gloves, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Shadoweave Gloves Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94305","cats":["crafting"]},"945":{"id":945,"t":"Therylune's Escape","lv":18,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Help Therylune escape, then tell Therysil at the Shrine of Aessina that her sister is safe.","desc":"Help!\nI was wandering around the Master's Glaive, and these dirty cultists surrounded me. Lucky I'm good at hiding!!\nCan you help me out of here? And I need to send word to my sister Therysil that I'm all right. She's in Ashenvale to the south, at the Shrine of Aessina.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"My sister was where?? Therylune doesn't mind getting herself dirty, but still! That's a long way to wander, and the Master's Glaive is an unwholesome place...\nWell thank you, ‹name›. It was very nice of you to let me know she's all right.\nDarkshore Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.6,"y":87.3,"n":"Therylune","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":22.6,"y":51.9,"n":"Therysil","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"97265":{"id":97265,"t":"Hate the hatefury","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat a variety of Hatefury satyr at Sargeron in Desolace and then return to Aka'rai in Shadowprey Village.\nHatefury Trickster slain : 0/ 2\nHatefury Hellcaller slain : 0/ 2\nHatefury Shadowstalker slain : 0/ 2\nHatefury Felsworn slain : 0/ 2\nHatefury Rogue slain : 0/ 2","desc":"Ever strike a deal with a satyr, mon?\nI have. How could I resist? The promise of power, knowledge far exceeding what any ordinary tome could offer... all alongside an eager and charismatic minion. What more could I ask for?\nBah, of course they would never bend the knee to a mortal. I bargained when I had nothing, only to be cast aside with even less.\nNow, I want revenge. Revenge against the Hatefury. Raid their camp to the northeast! Stain the dirt with their foul blood.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAka'rai's Tattered Vestments Dagger of Deals\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":25.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Aka'rai","s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7505":{"id":7505,"t":"Frost Shock and You","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nFrost Shock and You A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: Frost Shock and You","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: Frost Shock and You End Lorekeeper Javon Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Shaman Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7505","cats":["dire-maul"]},"7665":{"id":7665,"t":"Red Raptor Replacement","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Whistle of the Mottled Red Raptor","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Blue Raptor Swift Olive Raptor Swift Orange Raptor","back":"You bring me your old raptor, I give you new one with freshly sharpened claws! The new raptor will be just as fast as your old one, but with a new look to him. You can look at the swift raptors here to see what you will have to choose from.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.2,"y":75.6,"n":"Zjolnir","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"785":{"id":785,"t":"A strategic alliance","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Seek out Lar Prowltusk on the western flank of Sen'jin Village.","desc":"Thrall is a most wise and noble leader. His tenacity on the battlefield is matched only by his diplomatic tact.\nThe Darkspear Trolls have proven to be invaluable allies to orckind. Out of loyalty and honor we have sworn a pact of protection with them.\nThe Warchief has sent orders to make sure our Darkspear friends in Sen'jin Village are not under any direct threat. One of their most trusted scouts, Lar Prowltusk is keeping a close watch on their western flank.\nSeek out Lar and assist as needed.\nLevel 8 , requires level 5 Difficulty 5 6 11 14 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 785\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 8, 1,050 XP in all.\n1 [ 8 ] A Strategic Alliance this quest\nSeek out Lar Prowltusk on the western flank of Sen'jin Village.\n350 XP\n2 [ 8 ] Thwarting Kolkar Aggression\nLar Prowltusk outside of Sen'jin Village wants you to destroy the 3 sets of Attack Plans held within Kolkar Crag.\nLar Prowltusk Durotar\n700 XP","cats":["durotar"]},"225":{"id":225,"t":"The Weathered Grave","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.","desc":"The weathered grave marker reads simply:\nMORGAN LADIMORE\n<Upon further examination, you notice that dirt over the grave has been recently disturbed, and that a good amount of the dirt seems to have been displaced...>","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Morgan Ladimore?\nAhh, yes, of course. His was a long and sorrowful tale. I knew him, well, before he left for the war, but that was the last time I saw him. A noble and good man, he was, but he suffered a bad end.\nHere, I should have something here that can tell the tale better than my own recollections...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":17.7,"y":29.1,"n":"A Weathered Grave","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Sirra Von'Indi","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9665":{"id":9665,"t":"Bolstering Our Defenses","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Capture Crown Guard Tower, Eastwall Tower, Northpass Tower and Plaguewood Tower in the Eastern Plaguelands, then return to Emmisary Gormok at Light's Hope Chapel.\nCapture Crown Guard Tower\nCapture Eastwall Tower\nCapture Northpass Tower\nCapture Plaguewood Tower","desc":"Agents of the Forsaken uncovered an Alliance plot to establish new bases here in the Eastern Plaguelands, at abandoned towers throughout the area.\nIt is imperative that we not allow them to establish a significant presence on our eastern borders, and so we must stave off this Alliance incursion. Our current plans are to drive them out of any towers they may have already seized, and occupy those that we have under our control against further attacks.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"They must be fools to think that we would allow them to establish bases so close to one of our capitals.\nWe will bleed their numbers until they turn tail and retreat back to the south.","done":"This is good news, ‹name›. It will be a constant struggle here in the Plaguelands until we have fully driven back the forces of the Alliance.\nUntil that day, I hope that we will have your continued assistance.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.4,"y":47.9,"n":"Emmisary Gormok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9185":{"id":9185,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Rugged Armor Kit","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 25 Rugged Armor Kits and the Craftsman's Writ - Rugged Armor Kit - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Rugged Armor Kit\n25 Rugged Armor Kit Larion 10 % , Rabid Blisterpaw 0 % , Scorching Elemental 0 %\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Rugged Armor Kit","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order LW-448:\n25 Rugged Armor Kits.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"The rugged armor kits have many uses, ‹name›. They aren't JUST for slapping on certain armor pieces for added protection. Like this one here, I'm going to use it as teapot cozy.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5265":{"id":5265,"t":"The Argent Hold","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Open the Argent Hold and claim your reward.","desc":"Through the years the Argent Hold has remained locked. None have been worthy to reach inside and take from it the power of the Argent Dawn - until today.\nThe Argent Hold is now open to you, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArgent Avenger Argent Defender Argent Crusader\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"Whoa...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.4,"n":"Lord Maxwell Tyrosus","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.4,"n":"The Argent Hold","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6145":{"id":6145,"t":"The Crimson Courier","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Eastern Plaguelands and track down the Crimson Courier. Kill the Courier and recover the Grand Crusader's Command.\nTake the command to Nathanos Blightcaller for further instruction.\nThe Grand Crusader's Command Crimson Courier","desc":"Just as the body cannot survive without the head, the head cannot survive without the body. The defenses of the Scarlet Crusade's command inside Stratholme are almost impenetrable. We must, instead, cut the body out from under the head.\nMy Deathstalkers have been collecting data on the activity of the Crusade outside of Stratholme. Each day, a report is sent from their central command to Tyr's Hand. This report is the key, ‹race›! Find the Crimson Courier and recover that report. Return it to Nathanos.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Succeed now and you will have almost earned my respect, ‹class›.","done":"<Nathanos laughs.>\nExcellent! Finally! An opportunity to destroy the Scarlet Oracle!\nUndercity Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91745":{"id":91745,"t":"Mining consultant","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Talk to Kelsey Fargo outside the Echo Ridge Mine in Northshire Valley.","desc":"Go talk to the new mining apprentice, Kelsey Fargo. She works right outside the mine and has probably seen what the kobolds are up to. Maybe she can teach you a thing or two about mining while you're at it.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 0 silver, 25 copper Experience: 130\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Kobolds with books? Yah, I've seen kobolds running back and forth with books, yelling at each other. They must be stealing them from the library inside the abbey.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.2,"y":32.2,"n":"Kelsey Fargo","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3905":{"id":3905,"t":"Grape Manifest","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Grape Manifest to Brother Neals in Northshire Abbey.\nGrape Manifest\nProvided: Grape Manifest","desc":"Now that my crop is saved, take this Grape Manifest to Brother Neals. He manages the store of food and drink in Northshire, and I'm sure he'll be delighted to hear that he has fresh grapes.\nYou'll find Brother Neals in the abbey, in the bell tower... where he likes to taste his wine.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWine-stained Cloak Latched Belt\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You look to be in fine spirits! Come! Have a seat, and have a drink!","done":"Let's see here...\nOh my! Milly's grapes have been saved! When she told me that brigands overran her vineyards I nearly despaired, but my faith in the Light did not waver!\nAnd through your bravery, we now have grapes for more wine! May the Light bless you, ‹name›, and keep you safe!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":50.7,"y":39.3,"n":"Milly Osworth","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.5,"y":41.6,"n":"Brother Neals","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4465":{"id":4465,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":45.9,"y":85.2,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8465":{"id":8465,"t":"Speak to Salfa","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel through Timbermaw Hold and exit into Winterspring. Speak with Salfa, who stands guard outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold.","desc":"The threat of corruption comes not only from the Deadwood furbolgs to the south, but also from the east and the Winterfall furbolgs of Winterspring. If you wish to further aid us, speak with Salfa on the other side of the Hold, by the Winterspring entrance. Follow the path to the left to reach it.\nBe warned - if my kind inside considers you hostile or hated, they will attack. Travel as quick as you can, avoiding conflict. To kill a Timbermaw - even in self defense - will only alienate you further.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","done":"Greetings, ‹class› - I stand guard here as both a speaker for the Timbermaw here in Winterspring and as a defender of the tribe.\nOur Winterfall brethren here in this frigid land have fallen under the same corruptive sway as the furbolg of Felwood. If you've come here offering the Timbermaw furbolgs aid, then we are ready to accept such an offer.\nFelwood Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":64.8,"y":8.1,"n":"Nafien","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":27.7,"y":34.5,"n":"Salfa","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"6625":{"id":6625,"t":"Alliance Trauma","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Theramore in the Dustwallow Marsh and speak with Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen about joining the ranks of Alliance Trauma.","desc":"Doctor ‹name›, I presume. It is a pleasure to see you.\nI have some wonderful news for you! Gustaf VanHowzen, chief physician of Alliance Trauma has made a personal request for you to join him at Theramore. This could be the opportunity of a lifetime! I would give anything to be given a chance to study under the great doctor, Gustaf VanHowzen! Do not squander this opportunity, doctor!","rew":"Experience: 975","done":"Wonderful. Put on your scrubs, we are to start at once!\nDun Morogh Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.9,"y":30.4,"n":"Nissa Firestone","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":67.8,"y":49,"n":"Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen","e":1}],"cats":["first-aid"]},"8225":{"id":8225,"t":"Rare Fish - Brownell's Blue Striped Racer","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0. Pays 23s instead of 0.","obj":"Brownell's Blue Striped Racer","rew":"You will receive:\nNat Pagle's Extreme Anglin' Boots\nMoney: 23 0 gold, 23 silver, 0 copper","back":"*Whir* *Click*\nI seek rare fish for Fishmaster Bluegill to catalogue. If you bring me a Brownell's Blue Striped Racer, I will provide you with this fine reward.\n*Zzzap* *Whir*","done":"*Whir* Identification of Brownell's Racer complete. Your Reward is now available. *click* *click* *Bzzzz*","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":76.9,"n":"Fishbot 5000","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"2945":{"id":2945,"t":"Grime-Encrusted Ring","lv":34,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Figure out a way to remove the grime from the Grime-Encrusted Ring.\nGrime-Encrusted Ring Dark Iron Agent 10 %\nProvided: Grime-Encrusted Ring","desc":"You have uncovered what appears to be a ring from the corpse of one of the Dark Iron dwarves. It is difficult to tell what kind of ring it is, however; dirt and hardened residue cake the item completely, making wearing it impossible. You think you can make out the slight luster of precious metal and maybe even the glint of a gem under the residue.\nIf you are going to make use of this ring, you are going to need to find something to get the hardened residue off of it.","rew":"Experience: 2,700","back":"The gnomish contraption before you bears a plaque calling it \"The Sparklematic 5200\". The gist of the machine, from reading the instructions below the plaque, is to scrub away dirt that an item might have. The machine has a coin slot, accepting three silver coins to start the process once the item is placed inside it.\nIt would seem as though the grime-encrusted ring you found earlier is just the thing to try in this machine!","done":"You place the ring inside the Sparklematic 5200 and deposit a silver coin into the slot.\nPainful grinding noises emanate from the machine as it begins to jerk around violently. One can only guess what is happening with the ring inside the machine...\nThe machine suddenly stops, trumpeting its cessation with a simple \"Ding!\" The item receptacle opens up to reveal a small box that is neatly wrapped with a red bow. It would appear that the Sparklematic 5200 also gift wraps!\nStart an item: Grime-Encrusted Ring End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 34 , requires level 28 Difficulty 28 30 32 37 43 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 2945\nThe chain\n5 quests from level 34 to 35, 13,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 34 ] Grime-Encrusted Ring this quest\nFigure out a way to remove the grime from the Grime-Encrusted Ring.\nGrime-Encrusted Ring\n2,700 XP\n2 [ 34 ] Return of the Ring\nYou may either keep the ring, or you may find the person responsible for the imprint and engravings on the inside of the band.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,700 XP\n[ 34 ] Return of the Ring\nYou may either keep the ring, or you may find the person responsible for the imprint and engravings on the inside of the band.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,700 XP\n3 [ 35 ] Gnome Improvement\nBring the Brilliant Gold Ring, a Silver Bar, a Moss Agate, and 30 silver coins to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\nAfter: Return of the Ring\nTalvash del Kissel Dun Morogh\n2,750 XP\n[ 35 ] Nogg's Ring Redo\nBring the Brilliant Gold Ring, a Silver Bar, a Moss Agate, and 30 silver coins to Nogg in Orgrimmar.\nAfter: Return of the Ring\nNogg Orgrimmar\n2,750 XP","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"545":{"id":545,"t":"Dalaran Patrols","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Dalaran Summoners and 12 Elemental Slaves, then return to Magus Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\nDalaran Summoner slain : 0/ 6\nElemental Slave slain : 0/ 12","desc":"The wizards of Dalaran constructed a vast, magical dome around the heart of their city. Some believe it was for protection from the violence of these times, while others say they merely wanted solitude, to study and plot.\nI don't care what the reason was. I do care that the ruined outskirts of their city, outside the dome, may hide valuable magical treasures.\nBut the area is patrolled by the wizards and their elemental slaves.\nSo hunt them, and return when their numbers are sufficiently reduced.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you yet thinned the Dalaran patrols around their ruins?","done":"Very good. Those ruins should now be safe enough to search, if one is careful.\nThank you, ‹name›.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.6,"y":20.8,"n":"Magus Wordeen Voidglare","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6065":{"id":6065,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, I do believe you are ready...\nThunder Bluff Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":58.5,"y":88.3,"n":"Kary Thunderhorn","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9265":{"id":9265,"t":"Investigate the Scourge of the Undercity","lv":8,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 525 experience instead of 550, 0.95 times as much.","obj":"Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside the Undercity and investigate the glowing runic circles near their encampment.\n3 Dim Necrotic Stone Skeletal Soldier 35 % , Spectral Apparition 35 % , Spectral Spirit 31 % , Skeletal Trooper 31 %","desc":"The Lich King has sent his undead upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend the Undercity from these accursed invaders?\nThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you. Go!","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 525","back":"Have you investigated the invasion yet? There's no time for dawdling!","done":"Hmm. From what you've told me, the voices within the circles... they must be used for communication of some kind. I shudder to think what unnatural minds are contacted through such magic. Regardless, you seem to have emerged whole and sane. The Argent Dawn appreciates your service.\nTirisfal Glades Elwynn Forest Dun Morogh Mulgore Durotar Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.8,"y":69.7,"n":"Lieutenant Rukag","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8385":{"id":8385,"t":"Concerted Efforts","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor, 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor and 3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Ah, ‹name›. I hope you continue to lend your experience to the different battlefronts. A lot of our lads and lasses in the field look up to seasoned veterans like you.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with The League of Arathor\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"Ah, ‹name›. I hope you continue to lend your experience to the different battlefronts. A lot of our lads and lasses in the field look up to seasoned veterans like you.","done":"You live up to yer reputation, ‹name›. Without people like you, the Alliance wouldn't stand a chance against the savage forces of the Horde.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"7905":{"id":7905,"t":"The Darkmoon Faire","lv":60,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Free Ticket Voucher to Gelvas Grimgate, located inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival.\nFree Ticket Voucher\nProvided: Free Ticket Voucher","desc":"The Darkmoon Faire is coming! Be sure to experience all the wonders and excitement of it when it comes to town!\nIf you act right now, you can redeem this voucher for free prize tickets! Just hand your voucher to Gelvas Grimgate located inside the carnival.\nRight now, the Faire is outside Goldshire, in the Elwynn Forest. Don't miss out! Go today!","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Yes friend, may I help you? Do you have a voucher that needs redeeming?","done":"Welcome to the Darkmoon Faire! This voucher is good for FIVE, yes, FIVE prize tickets!\nWhen you accumulate prize tickets, you'll want to speak to me about redeeming them for valuable prizes. The more tickets you get, the more prizes you can win. Huzzah!\nDun Morogh Mulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.2,"y":33.7,"n":"Melnan Darkstone","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"385":{"id":385,"t":"Crocolisk Hunting","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get 5 pieces of Crocolisk Meat and 6 Crocolisk Skins for Marek Ironheart at the Farstrider Lodge.\n5 Crocolisk Meat Elder Saltwater Crocolisk 60.6 % , Wetlands Crocolisk 49.8 % , Saltwater Crocolisk 47.4 % , Loch Crocolisk 43.6 % and 4 more\n6 Crocolisk Skin Saltwater Crocolisk 80 % , Wetlands Crocolisk 80 % , Young Wetlands Crocolisk 80 % , Loch Crocolisk 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Many a hunter is attracted to Loch Modan to hunt our famous crocs. There are always merchants who seek out crocolisk skins for clothing items or armor, and there are also some who enjoy the taste of their meat.\nWe do some trade in this, but not a huge amount, as the crocolisks are ferocious and have entrenched themselves on the islands in the Loch. But don't let me dissuade you, it's quite an experience, wrestling with the jaws of the beasts.\nWhy, this one time...","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Crocolisk Steak Rugged Cape\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did I tell you about the time I almost lost my hand to one of the crocs? Nasty bugger it was, teeth like knives. But I was lucky... Jammed the brute's jaw shut with my knife. Still have the knife around here somewhere...","done":"Well now, these are excellent specimens you collected, ‹name›. Good money for high quality materials, that's for sure.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":81.8,"y":61.7,"n":"Marek Ironheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8865":{"id":8865,"t":"Festive Lunar Pant Suits","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFestive Black Pant Suit Festive Blue Pant Suit Festive Teal Pant Suit\nYou will also receive:\nLunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"I am please to inform you that I have a fine selection of festive pant suits available for you to own... but only in trade for coins of ancestry. If fashion is important to you, then these are what you're looking for! I assure you that you will not find pant suits like these anywhere else.\nIn exchange for some Coins of Ancestry, I will let you choose one of the three styles I have to keep as your own. Is this acceptable to you?","done":"Very well then - I accept these coins of ancestry. Please take your pant suit with my blessing. Also, please enjoy these complimentary fireworks.\nShould you have more coins of ancestry to trade, then speak with me again. I will be offering various items throughout the entirety of the Lunar Festival.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Valadar Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1185":{"id":1185,"t":"Under the Chitin Was...","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Hey, it's you again! Well, I mean you - as in the you that is ‹name›! Yes - that you!\nHey, let me start over!\nThat object you found in Silithus - it was in fact a book. It was a journal written in a very ancient dialect of what we now call the Darnassian tongue. It'll take a while, but I'm going to go over it very thoroughly. I thought you should know that what you found was extremely valuable for the Circle.\nThe den mother's all excited and everything!","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":44.9,"y":35.6,"n":"Umber","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"9105":{"id":9105,"t":"Plagueheart Circlet","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Plagueheart Circlet if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Circlet, 15 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 3 Mooncloth and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Circlet\n15 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Mooncloth\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Circlet\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Circlet.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"3505":{"id":3505,"t":"Betrayed","lv":53,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Blood Elf Reclaimers, and 10 Blood Elf Surveyors before seeking out Magus Rimtori's camp. Once you've found it, look for something that might be important to her that can be used to draw her into a fight.\nBlood Elf Reclaimer slain : 0/ 10\nBlood Elf Surveyor slain : 0/ 10","desc":"I thought as much.\nWe start our crusade against her workers along the southern bluffs on the northern peninsula of Azshara. Kill them with bloody rage--let them know they've betrayed the wrong allies.\nDo not concern yourself with her yet--she spends most of her time with her bodyguards searching Azshara. It would be prudent after you've slain her workers to find her personal camp. Scouting out where we can attack her would be wise. Perhaps there is something there we can use to provoke her.","rew":"Experience: 3,950\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The title of the book is emblazoned on the black leather cover in gold leaf--Kaldorei Tome of Summoning. As you open the pages you can see that the book is very old but in superb condition.\nYou assume the text is of some ancient language... perhaps Kaldorei?\nYour instincts tell you that you should return here once you've finished doling out retribution on the blood elves for their betrayal.","done":"You begin to skim some of the pages until you come to a page that's marked by a thin, black strip of silk cloth.\nAs you try to decipher the script, you see a diagram on the bottom of one of the pages. A quick look around at the scene before you and you realize that the crystals, the circle, and even some of the other components on the ground are set up in a similar pattern as the diagram.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.3,"y":51.5,"n":"Ag'tor Bloodfist","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":59.5,"y":31.3,"n":"Kaldorei Tome of Summoning","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"145":{"id":145,"t":"Messenger to Darkshire","lv":18,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Magistrate Solomon wants you to take a letter to Lord Ebonlocke in Darkshire.\nSolomon's Plea to Darkshire\nProvided: Solomon's Plea to Darkshire","desc":"I require your assistance once again. I have written to Lord Ebonlocke, requesting that he sends his trained guards, the Night Watch, to help with Lakeshire's defense. It is imperative this message makes it to him swiftly. You must exercise extreme caution. Ebonlocke is the mayor of Darkshire, in the heart of Duskwood. Do not stray from the roads.","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You appear to have traveled from afar, ‹class›. What business do you have here in Darkshire?","done":"Thank you for making the long journey here. This is indeed important information.\nRedridge Mountains Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":46.4,"n":"Lord Ello Ebonlocke","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"96785":{"id":96785,"t":"Aint no telling","lv":34,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find something within Stromgarde Keep to convince Anastasia to give up details of the secret deal.\nStolen Funds","desc":"Who do you think you are? Showing up and sticking your nose in official business.\nI'm not telling some rookie anything about the higher-up's dealings without good reason. Unless you've got something important, or valuable, for me, I've got nothing to say to you.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\nLevel 34 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 30 32 37 43 Side Both factions Class Rogue Quest ID 96785","cats":["rogue"]},"9025":{"id":9025,"t":"Morgan's Discovery","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Aristan Mottar outside the bank in Stormwind's Trade District.","desc":"Well, I'll be. It looks like Aristan might be on to something after all. I found traces of substances used in love potions and insidious mind-altering draughts.\nIt isn't unheard of for perfumes to have some of them, but a few of the ingredients I detected... Smells funny.","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Chocolates Handful of Rose Petals","done":"While I thought this would be the case, finding out that my suspicions were correct is still unsettling. We must carefully consider our next move.\nHere, to repay you for the purchase of the cologne and perfume.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Morgan Pestle","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":75,"n":"Aristan Mottar","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7025":{"id":7025,"t":"Treats for Greatfather Winter","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Gingerbread Cookies and an Ice Cold Milk to Greatfather Winter in Ironforge.\n5 Gingerbread Cookie\nIce Cold Milk Barrel of Milk , Foreman Silixiz 60 % , Wenikee Boltbucket 58.3 % , Takar the Seer 40 % and 4 more","desc":"Hey, can you do Greatfather Winter a favor, um, little boy/girl?\nNot to needlessly talk about myself in the third person, but Greatfather Winter has been at this all day and he could use a treat himself. Some gingerbread cookies and ice cold milk to wash them down with would really hit the spot. Think you could be a friend to the Greatfather and fetch some for me?","rew":"You will receive:\nSmokywood Pastures Gift Pack\nExperience: 1,650\n+25 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"All this talk of treats has given me a hankering for some myself. Mmmm... gingerbread cookies and milk...","done":"You're quite the helper to ol' Greatfather Winter there, ‹name›. Have a great Feast of Winter Veil.\nHere's a little something... you know, for the effort.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94465":{"id":94465,"t":"Call of fire","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.\nProvided: Torch of the Dormant Flame","desc":"Aye, ye've the strength to bear the totem o' fire, lad--but strength alone won't make ye ready.\nBeyond the Valley o' Kings, in the crags of Loch Modan, lies a hidden path to one o' our sacred peaks. There, Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame.\nTake this torch to him--it shows yer intent. Return it burnin' by the shrine's brazier, and I'll see ye earn the totem proper.","back":"Greetin's, Rhett. Ye've made it to the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame, eh? Not many do. Only those well-versed in the ‹class›'s path can grasp the secrets this place holds.\nShame ye came all this way just to be turned back--the climb's no stroll through Dun Morogh. But I'm the shrine's keeper, and I won't be lettin' just any foot trod about.","done":"Ah, me apologies, Rhett. Didn't spot the Torch in yer hand. An honor to meet ye proper.\nMany a wanderer climbs these heights chasin' tales of treasure or beasts, only to find naught but stone and silence. But we know better, don't we, Rhett?\nThis shrine holds truths far deeper than the Alliance can fathom. To us, it's a sacred flame that waits to be awakened.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":87.6,"y":43.6,"n":"Bruegs Kindleborn","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":32,"y":66,"n":"Braldir Ashmantle","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8305":{"id":8305,"t":"Long Forgotten Memories","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate the Crystalline Tear in Silithus and gaze into its depths.","desc":"In the southern desert of Silithus, near the sacred barrier, exists a single crystalline tear. This tear serves as a symbol of the great losses beset upon us during the War of the Shifting Sands. Locate this tear and gaze into its depths to gain enlightenment.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+50 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"You can feel a great sorrow revolving around this crystal. The force is so powerful that you feel as if you might collapse and die of sadness.\nTanaris Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":28.7,"y":89.1,"n":"Crystalline Tear","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8785":{"id":8785,"t":"The Orgrimmar Legion Needs Mojo!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Powerful Mojo, 6 Flasks of Big Mojo and 8 Oils of Immolation to Shadow Priestess Shai near Hive'Regal in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\n8 Oil of Immolation Molten Destroyer 0 % , Southsea Freebooter 0 % , Jadefire Betrayer 0 % , Bloodpetal Flayer 0 % and 2 more\n6 Flask of Big Mojo Mogh the Undying 25 % , Vilebranch Headhunter 9.8 % , Zanzil Witch Doctor 9.8 % , Cursed Atal'ai 9.8 % and 4 more\n6 Powerful Mojo Hakkar 25 % in Zul'Gurub , Jin'do the Hexxer 24 % in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir 24 % in Zul'Gurub , High Priest Venoxis 24 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nLogistics Task Briefing IV\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing IV","desc":"The Orgrimmar Legion has put in a request for several unusual ingredients. Given their current performance in Silithus, we'd like to comply with their request as soon as possible. Gather the materials and bring them to the troll called Shai.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Do you have my materials, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Just what I needed! I'll make a special concoction with this. The silithid won't like it one bit!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.3,"y":68.8,"n":"Shadow Priestess Shai","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78145":{"id":78145,"t":"Arcanic systems manual","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Arcanic Systems Manual","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nArcanic Systems Manual (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1265":{"id":1265,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search Sentry Point for any sign of Private Hendel.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Hendel? Yes, I know the man. But why would you need one of my soldiers?\nElling sent you to find him? Hmm, I don't like the sound of that. Elling wouldn't have you come to me first if your business wasn't troubling. I understand if you can't tell me what this is about, but know this: I have a duty to protect these lands. If you're going to cause a disturbance, then I suggest you inform me of whatever you can.\nI believe Hendel was stationed at the first tower outside of Theramore. Be cautious.","rew":"Experience: 280","back":"Yes, ‹name›?","done":"The man you seek, the one known as Hendel, is not here. Other sources have brought to the Lady Proudmoore information I believe you already know. She has asked me to find you, and give you aid in your venture. If you would allow it, I will tell you where to find Private Hendel so we can bring him to justice.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68,"y":48.7,"n":"Commander Samaul","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Archmage Tervosh","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"625":{"id":625,"t":"Cortello's Riddle","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Solve the riddle!","desc":"A far off land in Kalimdor awaits\nWhere peril has dashed hopes and fates\nEast of Barrens the weather is harsh\nGloom and danger pock Dustwallow Marsh\nBut there lies a clue for those up to the test\nWaiting to be found in a cave in the southwest","rew":"Experience: 3,600","done":"You find a musty scroll.\nSwamp of Sorrows Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":22.9,"y":48.2,"n":"A Soggy Scroll","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":31.1,"y":66.1,"n":"Musty Scroll","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8065":{"id":8065,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Haruspex's Tunic","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Tabard. Maywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale. You must also be Revered with Zandalar.\nPrimal Hakkari Tabard\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The ultimate symbol of a haruspex's power is what they wear, ‹name›. Of these, the tunic symbolizes the connection between themselves and the divine wisdom they seek. It often weaves parts of the beasties they sacrifice into the tunic; this reminds them of the connection they have to their gifts.\nBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us. Do this, and a tunic seeping with the true power of a haruspex is yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Haruspex's Tunic\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Got the necessary Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub? The haruspex's tunic is well worth any effort ya be needin' to make.","done":"Impressive... you've successfully collected the required Paragons of Power, ‹name›. Your accomplishments in Zul'Gurub for the Zandalar are legendary; hence forth, you'll be revered amongst the tribe. Here is your tunic, mighty ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8945":{"id":8945,"t":"Dead Man's Plea","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go into Stratholme and rescue Ysida Harmon from Baron Rivendare.\nYsida Freed","desc":"I'll provide you the information you ask for, ‹name›. But more pressing matters are at hand.\nMy beloved wife has been taken prisoner by Rivendare's undead scum.\nI strongly objected to her joining the Argent Dawn's foolish crusade, yet that's not of importance anymore. You must finish what I attempted to do, you must rescue Ysida from the clutches of the Baron!","rew":"You will receive:\nYsida's Satchel\nExperience: 8,300","done":"Thank you for rescuing me... I feared for my life. Please accept this as a small token of my gratitude.\nAnthion is... no... he can't be...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"93585":{"id":93585,"t":"This light of mine","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Escort Father Tuttle to The Harborage.\nEscort Father Tuttle to The Harborage","desc":"Oh thank goodness, someone civilized!\nI came here on behalf of the Church of the Holy Light to make contact with the draenei of the Harborage. The Alliance has no foothold here, you see, and a bit of diplomacy with the locals may help us in that regard. The Light welcomes all into its fold, after all!\nHowever, the road past this bridge is crawling with the draenei's more savage kin. If I am to make it to the Harborage safely, I will need protection. Would you aid me, ‹class›?","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":22,"y":50.6,"n":"Father Tuttle","s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"1425":{"id":1425,"t":"Deliver the Shipment","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Shipment to Nethergarde to Quartermaster Lungertz in Nethergarde Keep.\nShipment to Nethergarde\nProvided: Shipment to Nethergarde","desc":"While I fix this wagon, ‹name›, I have one last task for you.\nI have packed the most vital supplies saved from the ogre attacks. Take them to Nethergarde Keep. The keep is nestled in the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, keeping watch over the Dark Portal.\nTo reach Nethergard, follow the road east. When it branches head south into the Blasted Lands, then turn left at the next fork. Follow the road, ‹name›, and be wary.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have business with me?","done":"What? A package from Biggs' caravan? We thought it, and he, were lost.\nThank you, ‹name›. With luck, these supplies will carry the much needed reagent, Azoran Crystals. Our stock is running low...\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":26.7,"y":59.8,"n":"Watcher Biggs","s":1},{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.5,"y":21.4,"n":"Quartermaster Lungertz","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"98065":{"id":98065,"t":"Crown of the earth","lv":11,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Moonwell Remnants to Tyrande Whisperwind in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.\nProvided: Moonwell Remnants","desc":"You must bring this to Tyrande at once! I will transfer it to a more ceremonial container for you.\nDo not be afraid. The High Priestess of Elune is firm, but kind. She protects all who enter Darnassus, and carries our goddess' light to all.\nShe will be glad to receive this sacred water. You will find her directly above us.","back":"Please state your business. I have a city to run, and a people to lead.","done":"Staghelm has done much in my beloved's absence, but he is not Malfurion. And he does not run the affairs of Darnassus--that burden is mine alone.\n<Tyrande's face settles.>\nI apologize. As you have likely seen, we have many challenges to overcome.\nFandral is Arch Druid for now, and I ask you respect his station. But his doings pertain to druidism, and mine not only to Elune but indeed to lead our people as she wills.\nEvery drop of this water is blessed by our goddess. I thank you for saving it.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":40.2,"y":88.4,"n":"Lariia","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39,"y":81.2,"n":"Tyrande Whisperwind","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"6385":{"id":6385,"t":"Doras the Wind Rider Master","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gryshka's Letter to Doras in Orgrimmar.\nGryshka's Letter\nProvided: Gryshka's Letter","desc":"I've written a letter of thanks to Zargh. Will you deliver it for me? If you've already been to the Crossroads and spoken with their wind rider master, then you can fly a wind rider back there.\nTake my letter to Doras, the wind rider master of Orgrimmar, and speak with him about transport to the Crossroads.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Do you need one of my wind riders?","done":"You have to get this to the Crossroads in the Barrens? Yes, I can get you there...","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":54.1,"y":68.4,"n":"Innkeeper Gryshka","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":45.1,"y":63.9,"n":"Doras","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"865":{"id":865,"t":"Raptor Horns","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 5 Intact Raptor Horns from Sunscale Scytheclaws, and bring them to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\n5 Intact Raptor Horn Sunscale Scytheclaw 80 % , Ishamuhale 80 % , Takk the Leaper 80 %","desc":"The raptors of the Barrens are smarter than raptors in other lands. And I think all that smarts is hiding in their horns! If so, then I could grind their horns into powder and use it to make \"smart drinks.\" I could sell them for a fortune!!!\nAnd you can help me. Find me intact raptor horns from sunscale scytheclaws. They roam in the southern Barrens, and in the northern Barrens near the border of Ashenvale Forest.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Raptor Punch Barkeeper's Cloak\nExperience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Did you get the horns, ‹name›? Those things are going to make me a fortune!","done":"Great, you got them! Now I just need to ground them down and mix them with some wine, and...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":37.6,"n":"Mebok Mizzyrix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4865":{"id":4865,"t":"Serpent Wild","lv":26,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report your findings to Motega Firemane.","desc":"If I did not see that with my own eyes I would never have believed it to be true. Vengeance has come to Thousand Needles!\n<Hagar wipes his brow.>\n‹name›, you must act quickly! Go now and seek out Motega Firemane; he is located at Whitereach Post just northwest of Freewind Post along the road. He will know what to do!","rew":"Experience: 1,050\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Vengeance! So, the legend of Arikara is true. Indeed, this is a problem that must be resolved immediately.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":44.6,"y":50.3,"n":"Hagar Lightninghoof","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.5,"y":32.3,"n":"Motega Firemane","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1105":{"id":1105,"t":"Hardened Shells","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 9 Hardened Tortoise Shells to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\n9 Hardened Tortoise Shell Sparkleshell Tortoise 30 % , Sparkleshell Snapper 30 % , Sparkleshell Borer 30 %","desc":"My brother is working on a new fuel for his rocket car. He's brilliant, he really is. So brilliant that... I think that new fuel he's designing is strong enough to eat right through the car's chassis!\nI want to reinforce its fuel tanks before that happens.\nThe tortoises out on the flats have very hard shells. I want to use them to create new tanks for our rocket car. Tanks that can hold my brother's new fuel.\nYou look responsible enough. Will you get me those shells?","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450","back":"My brother is making progress with his new fuel design, and that has me worried. I need to start work on a tortoise shell fuel tank as soon as possible!","done":"You got them! Thanks, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Wizzle Brassbolts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7825":{"id":7825,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of Thunder Bluff.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of Thunder Bluff, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":43,"y":42.7,"n":"Rumstag Proudstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"98545":{"id":98545,"t":"Leonids letter","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Sealed Letter to Glix Xizzix in the Undercity.\nProvided: Sealed Letter","desc":"Since you are here, I'd like you to deliver this letter to an old friend of mine in the Undercity. I'd deliver myself but I have a somewhat colorful history with the Dark Lady, and it would be better if a neutral third party made the delivery.\nYou are looking for a goblin named Glix Xizzix in the Trade Quarter area of the Undercity. I'm sure he'd be happy to compensate you for your time.\n<Leonid lets out a low chuckle as he hands you the letter.>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTim's Lost Rib Mug of Muddled Memories Misplaced Shooter\nExperience: 90\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"What's that? You say that Leonid sent you? Oh boy, haven't seen that crusty old soldier since Naxxramas was raining hell down on our heads.","done":"Thanks for delivering this, pal.\nWait... he said I'd tip you? I didn't agree to that!\nFine. Take your pick of this junk in the lost and found. You'd be surprised how many of these Forsaken leave their stuff laying around after getting haircuts. There's a joke here about them being brainless, but I suspect in a lot of cases it might actually be true.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.8,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":69.8,"y":47,"n":"Glix Xizzix","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4145":{"id":4145,"t":"Larion and Muigin","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hunt 5 Bloodpetal Lashers, 5 Bloodpetal Threshers, 5 Bloodpetal Flayers and 5 Bloodpetal Trappers for Larion at Marshal's Refuge.\nBloodpetal Lasher slain : 0/ 5\nBloodpetal Trapper slain : 0/ 5\nBloodpetal Flayer slain : 0/ 5\nBloodpetal Thresher slain : 0/ 5","desc":"See Muigin over there? It's HIS fault we're lost!\nI'm the one that knew the way, but he insisted he knew a shortcut, and we ended up here!\nTo make matters worse, now he keeps sending his crazy plant pests to annoy me. I'm so angry that I'm not planning on talking to him any time soon, but these pests are too much to handle.\nWhy don't we try to limit his supply, first thing. Go out and hunt some Bloodpetals, then return to me.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100","back":"Muigin needs to apologize first before I'll talk to him again!","done":"Thanks for your help, ‹name›, but I'm afraid I have some bad news...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":45.5,"y":8.7,"n":"Larion","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4385":{"id":4385,"t":"Crystal Charge","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Red Power Crystal Red Power Crystal , Red Power Crystal , Mor'vek 46.2 % , Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more\n10 Yellow Power Crystal Yellow Power Crystal , Yellow Power Crystal , Mor'vek 66.7 % , Gruff 0.6 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Crystal Charge","back":"The Pylon table allows you to combine red power crystals with yellow power crystals.\nAccording to J.D.'s manual, this combination can be used to create a large explosion that can inflict damage on your enemies.","done":"Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.\nThe resulting combination is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":56.5,"y":12.5,"n":"Northern Crystal Pylon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"97985":{"id":97985,"t":"Thundering hearts","lv":33,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay Stormheart in Thousand Needles and acquire its heart.\nStormheart's Still-beating Heart","desc":"Fascinating, aren't they? This is the first time I have ever been privy to the secrets of abomination creation.\nI have been studying these notes, and it appears we need a heart. A massive one!\nI hear there is a thunder lizard there of impressive size called Stormheart, that patrols along the canyon edge in Thousand Needles. With a name like that it must have the perfect heart. I must have that heart!\nOh, also I suggest you bring friends. Stormheart isn't known for being docile.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity\nUndercity Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":49.2,"y":70.4,"n":"Calder Gray","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"3105":{"id":3105,"t":"Tainted Letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Tainted Letter and speak to Drusilla La Salle next to Northshire Abbey.\nTainted Letter\nProvided: Tainted Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Drusilla, one of our local trainers. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, so you've arrived, and not a moment too soon, ‹name›. Some of the guards were over here a moment ago and were giving me curious looks... pathetic mundanes.","done":"As you grow in power, you will be tempted--you must always remember to control yourself. I will not lie--corruption can come to any practitioner of the arcane; especially one who deals with creatures from the Twisting Nether. Be patient, and be prudent... but do not let that repress your ambition.\nAs you grow more powerful, return to me and I will teach you more about our ways.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.9,"y":42.6,"n":"Drusilla La Salle","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4785":{"id":4785,"t":"Fine Gold Thread","lv":37,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFine Gold Thread","done":"Here you go, ‹name›. And please tell Menara we say hello.\nWe expect great things of you. Perhaps when the Legion falls to its knees, your name will be spoken aloud and in praise of your power. I can't wait!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.7,"y":76.9,"n":"Xizk Goodstitch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1665":{"id":1665,"t":"Bartleby's Mug","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Bartleby's Mug to Burlguard\nBartleby's Mug\nProvided: Bartleby's Mug","desc":"Ok, here's my mug. Wait! Let me finish what's in it first... there we go.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"I saw your fight with Bartleby. Nicely done! Did you get his mug?","done":"There it is! He sure didn't want to part with it, but you were persuasive. Well done.\nNow for your lesson...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.8,"y":52.5,"n":"Bartleby","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":53.3,"n":"Harry Burlguard","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1505":{"id":1505,"t":"Veteran Uzzek","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Uzzek at Far Watch Post.","desc":"The Horde honors its warriors because their strength is unquestioned. But the truly great warriors are great students as well.\nSeek out Uzzek. He is a veteran of many battles and now instructs young warriors in the ways of combat. You will find him south of Far Watch Post, the orc garrison on the border of the Barrens and Durotar.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Hello, young one. Here for some instruction, are you?\nDurotar Mulgore Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.2,"y":42.4,"n":"Tarshaw Jaggedscar","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":49.4,"y":60.4,"n":"Krang Stonehoof","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.2,"y":32.4,"n":"Sorek","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":57.6,"y":87.2,"n":"Torm Ragetotem","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":61.4,"y":21,"n":"Uzzek","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1825":{"id":1825,"t":"Speak with Thun'grim","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens.","desc":"Thun'grim Firegaze, an orc blacksmith of renown, has heard of your continued deeds of valor in service of the Horde. He would like to fashion for you a suit of armor, and bids you speak with him immediately.\nThun'grim is camped east of the Crossroads in the Barrens.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"Yes, you have come. This is good, for we have much to discuss, you and I.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.7,"y":59.4,"n":"Ruga Ragetotem","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5505":{"id":5505,"t":"The Key to Scholomance","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSkeleton Key\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Well, here you are, ‹name› - the completed Skeleton Key. I am certain as I can be that this key will allow you within the confines of the Scholomance. There's only one way to be absolutely sure it works, though. Waste no time in trying it out, I say.\nGood luck, mighty hero. May you continue to bring light unto the darkness!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":83.8,"n":"Alchemist Arbington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"65":{"id":65,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to talk to Wiley in Lakeshire.","desc":"The band of wretches responsible for driving the good people of Westfall from the land call themselves The Defias Brotherhood. I need you to infiltrate this clan of thugs. We need to know who heads up the cartel and where they are hiding out. In Lakeshire, in the inn, there is a rogue by the name of Wiley who owes me a favor.\nTravel to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, east of Elwynn, and find out what you can.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"So, Stoutmantle sent you? Well, I owe him.\nWestfall Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.4,"y":45.3,"n":"Wiley the Black","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"305":{"id":305,"t":"In Search of The Excavation Team","lv":24,"min":21,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from In Search of The Excavation Team.","obj":"Tarrel Rockweaver wants you to travel to the Excavation Site and contact Merrin Rockweaver.","desc":"You cannot imagine how worried I have been.\nMy wife, Merrin, has been sending me letters each week for the past month. She is part of the Whelgar Excavation team. But it has been nearly two weeks since her last correspondence. Surely something is wrong!\nLongbraid said that he would send a scout to check up on things if we did not hear from the team soon. I assume that scout is you, ‹name›. Find Merrin at the excavation site to the east!","rew":"Experience: 975\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Oh, thank the heavens you are here!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.5,"y":52.2,"n":"Tarrel Rockweaver","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.9,"y":52.3,"n":"Merrin Rockweaver","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"465":{"id":465,"t":"Nek'rosh's Gambit","lv":31,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy the Dragonmaw catapults.\nDwarven Tinder Chieftain Nek'rosh\nProvided: Dwarven Tinder","desc":"While you were fighting the Dragonmaws, we discovered more of their plans.\nNek'rosh has built catapults and aims to lay siege to Menethil! And with the fighting in Dun Algaz, we're effectively blocked from reinforcements!\nYou need to take out those catapults. They're in the Dragonmaw encampment.\nHere, take this tinder. Fight your way to the catapults and light them with the tinder.\nAnd after you've done that, find and kill Nek'rosh. We need to cut this Dragonmaw beast down...at its neck.","rew":"Experience: 1,900\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The first catapult is before you. Will you set it aflame?","done":"You place some of the tinder on the catapult then strike a spark onto it.\nFlame erupts and quickly spreads!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.9,"y":57.5,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":47.5,"y":47,"n":"Dragonmaw Catapult","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92465":{"id":92465,"t":"Agitators","lv":3,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 6 Roiling Winds and 7 Al'Aketh Converts in Thendal Grove.\nAl'Aketh Convert slain : 0/ 7\nRoiling Winds destroyed : 0/ 6","desc":"The Al'Aketh cult is a blight upon this island. These cultists are surely the ones responsible for agitating the simple wind sprites that reside here and turning them violent.\nRegrettably, we'll need to disperse these roiling winds here before they harm someone. We also need to send a clear message to the cult that they are not welcome in the grove.\nWill you lend me your aid, ‹class›?","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 250\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"It pains me to shed shen'dorei blood here in the grove, but we do what we must.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":47.2,"y":21.8,"n":"Yala Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2865":{"id":2865,"t":"Scarab Shells","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Uncracked Scarab Shells to Tran'rek in Gadgetzan.\n5 Uncracked Scarab Shell Scarab 80 % in Zul'Farrak","desc":"The scarabs of Tanaris have very hard shells! Hard enough to use as a building material for lots of things. So many things!\nIn fact, those shells are so useful... the scarabs were hunted all to near extinction!\nI know where there are more scarabs, and if you promise to bring me their shells then I'll tell you where they are. Promise?\nOk, the scarabs have a colony in Zul'Farrak. I guess the trolls don't hunt them for their shells.\nBut you can! Go to Zul'Farrak and get me uncracked shells!","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Do you have the shells? My cousin in Booty Bay is waiting for a load of them, and he's getting impatient!","done":"Oh, great! You got them!\nThanks, ‹name›. You're a real lifesaver!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.6,"y":26.8,"n":"Tran'rek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8145":{"id":8145,"t":"The Maelstrom's Tendril","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nMaelstrom's Tendril\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","done":"Amongst the Zandalarians, the profession of ‹class› is revered. Our greatest hunters travel to the edge of the Maelstrom to prove their resolution.\nFrom the heart of the sea they pull strands of kelp known as Maelstrom Tendrils. The kelp is then woven into a talisman that is enchanted to improve their accuracy and power.\nI now grant you a single weaving of the Maelstrom's Tendril. As your bond with Zandalar grows, I shall weave more power into the talisman.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});